sequenceDiagram
  %% Current workflow and delivery gate: stage 4 of the command development pipeline. Open one PR only after stages 1 to 3 have produced the spec-first branch, working feature and passing end-to-end proof. CI confirms that result. CI proof is deliberately disabled by ORBIT_PROOF_ENABLED until commands have been checked systematically; a green CI result while it is off is not proof coverage.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: development pipeline stage 4 · complete PR, CI and gate
  %% kind: pipeline.4-pr-and-ci
  autonumber
  %% lane AG icon=terminal pill=author tone=gray
  %% lane RV icon=terminal pill=reviewer tone=amber
  %% lane GH icon=server pill=PR tone=purple
  %% lane CI icon=workflow pill=checks tone=green
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  participant AG as Author<br/>proven feature
  participant RV as Reviewer<br/>fresh subagent
  participant GH as GitHub<br/>PR · main
  participant CI as CI<br/>selected checks
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>delivery gate
  AG->>RV: Review the complete diff<br/>spec · code · proof evidence
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the branch's first commit holds the chart, page and cases; implementation and required end-to-end proof have passed in one task copy with its nested fleet
  %%> - use the plug-in point checklist where applicable; fix findings before opening or updating the PR
  RV-->>AG: Findings or clean review<br/>independent assessment
  AG->>GH: Push and open one PR<br/>complete feature · into main
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - no draft or ready PR opened before the feature and its proof passed
  %%> - the PR body states the independent review ran, the proof result and any limits; a draft can hold back already-proven work, not replace pre-PR proof
  GH->>CI: Run selected checks<br/>immutable PR merge tree
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - scopes checks by changed inputs; Required checks aggregates every selected required result
  %%> - the pre-check: it plans the fixture shards and starts none; the merge queue run starts them
  opt CI proof enabled and selected
    Note over CI: Check proof trust<br/>ORBIT_PROOF_ENABLED=true
    %%> When:
    %%> - deliberately off until commands have been checked systematically; this documentation does not enable it
    %%> - when enabled, selection.txt selects commands; outside PRs also need maintainer approval of the exact head and the run-proofs label
    CI->>GW: Confirm the proven head<br/>proof:run COMMIT
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the trusted CI caller supplies the SHA; proof:run selects cases and uses copies of the proof Project's default container Instance, each with its nested fleet
    %%> - each copy brings in the commit and checks its workspace; assigned batches reset the fleet before the first batch and after a batch that can change it
    %%> - cases and runner are the same as the author's proof; no merge-base replay runs in copies
    %%> - a new push cancels the previous PR proof; each run end requests destruction of its copy
    GW-->>CI: Verdict per case<br/>complete selected coverage
    %%> Result:
    %%> - a selected proof that runs blocks Required checks; failed, unrun, missing or interrupted coverage cannot pass
  end
  alt every required check passes
    CI-->>GH: Required checks<br/>green on the head
    %%> Result:
    %%> - CI confirms an already-proven feature; with CI proof off, green does not establish proof coverage
    AG->>GH: Request the merge gate<br/>review of exact head
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - task-copy publication does not automatically merge; follow the Project's review and merge policy
    %%> - task:pr-merge is unavailable for task copies; its older gate applies only to groups it supports
    %%> - a new head needs affected local checks and proofs, CI and the gate again
    AG->>GH: Queue the pull request<br/>gh pr merge --squash --auto
    %%> Requirements:
    %%> - green CI and the authorized review on the exact head; publication or a green result alone does not authorize a merge
    %%> - --match-head-commit names the reviewed head, so GitHub refuses a head that moved; no branch update because main moved
    GH->>CI: Run the merge queue run<br/>the commit main receives
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - GitHub builds one squash commit on main and any pull request still ahead; this run adds the selected fixture shards
    %%> - the Docs gate reads the pull request body again
    %%> - the plan covers changes since the newest commit that the queue tests or main delivered
    alt the queue run passes
      CI-->>GH: Required checks<br/>green on the queue commit
      Note over GH: Fast-forward main<br/>to the tested commit
      GH->>CI: Check main delivery<br/>queue run · release inputs
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - finds the green queue run on the exact main commit and promotes its web build; it compares no trees
      %%> - a red main is fixed forward and never released; stages 5 and 6 confirm and refresh the working result
    else the queue run fails
      CI--xGH: Required checks<br/>red · leaves the queue
      GH--xAG: Fix and queue again<br/>same branch · same PR
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the next queued pull request is tested on main without it
    end
  else a required check fails
    CI--xGH: Required checks<br/>red · no merge
    GH--xAG: Fix and prove again<br/>same branch · same PR
    %%> Result:
    %%> - fix failures caused by the change; report unrelated main failures without treating them as a passing check
  end
